WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.629 --> 00:00:03.631
Jim Acosta has the day off.

00:00:03.631 --> 00:00:04.432
You are in the CNN newsroom.

00:00:04.565 --> 00:00:07.168
We begin this hour with breaking

00:00:07.301 --> 00:00:07.635
news.

00:00:07.635 --> 00:00:09.303
Former president Jimmy Carter is

00:00:09.637 --> 00:00:11.639
receiving hospice care at his

00:00:11.639 --> 00:00:13.908
home in plains, Georgia.

00:00:14.041 --> 00:00:15.042
Sources tell CNN president Biden

00:00:15.176 --> 00:00:17.645
is staying in close contact with

00:00:17.645 --> 00:00:18.512
the family.

00:00:18.646 --> 00:00:20.748
Let's go now to CNN's Jeff

00:00:20.881 --> 00:00:22.416
Zeleny in Washington.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:23.951
What more have you learned since

00:00:24.085 --> 00:00:26.721
we've just heard this not too

00:00:26.854 --> 00:00:27.154
long ago.

00:00:27.288 --> 00:00:27.888
&gt;&gt; We are learning this this

00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:30.658
afternoon and the Carter center

00:00:30.791 --> 00:00:32.793
advised something we had not

00:00:32.927 --> 00:00:34.261
known, the former president has

00:00:34.395 --> 00:00:35.896
had a brief series of hospital

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:36.197
stays.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:37.832
He made the decision to spend

00:00:37.965 --> 00:00:40.368
his final days to enter hospice

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:41.902
care in plains, Georgia.

00:00:42.036 --> 00:00:43.404
That is really so extraordinary

00:00:43.671 --> 00:00:44.305
because that of course is where

00:00:44.438 --> 00:00:47.241
the former president has sent

00:00:47.675 --> 00:00:47.875
his entire life with the

00:00:48.009 --> 00:00:49.076
exception, of course, of his

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.679
four years here in Washington at

00:00:51.812 --> 00:00:52.913
the white house as well as his

00:00:53.047 --> 00:00:54.115
military service as a young man.

00:00:54.248 --> 00:00:56.651
He went home to plains, Georgia,

00:00:56.784 --> 00:00:57.685
in his post-presidency, and

00:00:57.818 --> 00:01:00.287
that's where he's been ever

00:01:00.421 --> 00:01:00.588
since.

00:01:00.721 --> 00:01:03.024
With rose Lynn, his wife at his

00:01:03.157 --> 00:01:04.725
side for 77 years of marriage or

00:01:04.859 --> 00:01:04.992
so.

00:01:05.126 --> 00:01:05.960
So the family is saying that he

00:01:06.093 --> 00:01:08.162
is going to be in hospice care,

00:01:08.295 --> 00:01:09.830
and we are also learning just a

00:01:09.964 --> 00:01:11.699
short time ago, we heard from

00:01:11.699 --> 00:01:14.101
his grandson, a former Georgia

00:01:14.235 --> 00:01:15.903
state senator, a gubernatorial

00:01:16.037 --> 00:01:16.937
candidate, who is basically in

00:01:17.071 --> 00:01:18.506
the family business in Georgia,

00:01:18.639 --> 00:01:20.708
Jason Carter, and he said he

00:01:20.841 --> 00:01:22.076
visited with his grandparents

00:01:22.209 --> 00:01:22.610
yesterday in plains.

00:01:22.743 --> 00:01:23.711
He tweets this.

00:01:23.711 --> 00:01:26.080
I saw both of my grandparents

00:01:26.213 --> 00:01:26.447
yesterday.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.082
They're at peace, and as always,

00:01:28.215 --> 00:01:29.950
their home is full of love.

00:01:30.084 --> 00:01:31.986
Thank you for all of your kind

00:01:32.119 --> 00:01:32.319
words.

00:01:32.453 --> 00:01:34.221
As I'm talking to you, former

00:01:34.355 --> 00:01:35.723
advisers to the Carter family,

00:01:35.723 --> 00:01:36.824
they're really keeping a close

00:01:36.957 --> 00:01:39.727
hold on his impact held

00:01:39.727 --> 00:01:40.761
condition.

00:01:40.895 --> 00:01:43.731
Instead, they are choosing to

00:01:43.864 --> 00:01:45.132
talk about his life, really his

00:01:45.266 --> 00:01:47.168
extraordinary legacy from peanut

00:01:47.301 --> 00:01:48.636
farmer to the presidency, and it

00:01:48.769 --> 00:01:51.372
was really the post presidency,

00:01:51.739 --> 00:01:53.074
the last half century nearly of

00:01:53.207 --> 00:01:55.142
his work that has been so

00:01:55.276 --> 00:01:56.777
extraordinary, and he's been a

00:01:56.911 --> 00:01:58.112
Sunday schoolteacher, a parade

00:01:58.245 --> 00:01:59.113
of people we're seeing right

00:01:59.246 --> 00:02:02.016
here now, his plains, Georgia,

00:02:02.149 --> 00:02:02.650
church.

00:02:02.783 --> 00:02:03.751
He's greeting visitors,

00:02:03.851 --> 00:02:04.752
something he always did, if he

00:02:04.885 --> 00:02:06.487
was on an airplane, he was known

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.456
to be shaking hands with

00:02:08.589 --> 00:02:09.890
passengers up and down the

00:02:10.024 --> 00:02:10.324
aisle.

00:02:10.458 --> 00:02:11.826
He taught Sunday school, built

00:02:11.959 --> 00:02:13.828
homes for habitat for humanity,

00:02:13.961 --> 00:02:14.895
particularly in the wake of

00:02:15.029 --> 00:02:15.830
hurricane Katrina.

00:02:15.963 --> 00:02:16.964
I certainly remember that well.

00:02:17.098 --> 00:02:17.765
Clearly now, president Biden,

00:02:17.898 --> 00:02:20.067
I'm told, has been advised of

00:02:20.201 --> 00:02:21.769
this, and he is in close contact

00:02:21.769 --> 00:02:23.304
as well, and some interesting

00:02:23.437 --> 00:02:25.239
history between those men as

00:02:25.372 --> 00:02:25.773
well.

00:02:25.773 --> 00:02:26.273
President Biden paid a visit to

00:02:26.407 --> 00:02:28.008
the Carters on the 100th day of

00:02:28.142 --> 00:02:32.246
his presidency, back in 2021,

00:02:32.379 --> 00:02:33.781
and then senator Joe Biden was

00:02:33.914 --> 00:02:36.617
the first senator to endorse the

00:02:36.751 --> 00:02:39.286
Carter presidential bid, back in

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:39.787
1976.

00:02:39.787 --> 00:02:41.322
So they have a long history

00:02:41.455 --> 00:02:41.789
there.

00:02:41.789 --> 00:02:42.757
I'm told the white house is in

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:43.791
close contact.

00:02:43.791 --> 00:02:48.963
They share some actual former

00:02:49.096 --> 00:02:50.297
advisers.

00:02:50.431 --> 00:02:51.799
Anita Dunn was a young adviser

00:02:51.799 --> 00:02:53.834
to Jimmy Carter, all thoughts

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:58.372
are with the Carters.

00:02:58.506 --> 00:02:59.106
For now, he has chosen to remain

00:02:59.240 --> 00:02:59.807
in plains, Georgia, the

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:01.008
epicenter of his life, his

00:03:01.142 --> 00:03:02.710
legacy felt around the world,

00:03:02.843 --> 00:03:03.043
Sarah.

00:03:03.177 --> 00:03:04.345
&gt;&gt; I have to say, I met him when

00:03:04.478 --> 00:03:05.813
I was in college.

00:03:05.813 --> 00:03:08.315
I know many of you have met and

00:03:08.449 --> 00:03:08.783
talked to them.

00:03:08.916 --> 00:03:10.284
He was gracious, he was kind.

00:03:10.417 --> 00:03:11.819
He was giving.

00:03:11.952 --> 00:03:14.955
It was remarkable to be in his

00:03:15.089 --> 00:03:15.823
presence because of all the

00:03:15.823 --> 00:03:19.226
things he's done, not just being

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:19.827
the president.

00:03:19.827 --> 00:03:22.363
Really it's the post presidency

00:03:22.496 --> 00:03:22.663
work.

00:03:22.797 --> 00:03:25.232
Lots of prayers for his family.

00:03:25.366 --> 00:03:26.867
Jeff Zeleny, thank you so much

00:03:27.001 --> 00:03:29.837
for joining us.

00:03:29.937 --> 00:03:32.873
&gt;&gt;&gt; Let's turn to kye burr,

00:03:33.007 --> 00:03:36.076
author of "The unfinished

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:39.847
presidency of Jimmy Carter,"

00:03:39.847 --> 00:03:40.881
when was the last time you were

00:03:41.015 --> 00:03:42.616
able to speak and see the former

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:43.884
president and how was he doing

00:03:44.018 --> 00:03:44.518
at that time?

00:03:44.652 --> 00:03:45.986
&gt;&gt; The last time I saw

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.956
presidential Carter was July of

00:03:49.089 --> 00:03:51.225
2021 at his 75th wedding

00:03:51.358 --> 00:03:52.193
anniversary, which was a gala

00:03:52.326 --> 00:03:54.528
event in plains, where he

00:03:54.662 --> 00:03:57.898
invited 350 colleagues and

00:03:58.032 --> 00:04:00.201
friends and politicians like

00:04:00.334 --> 00:04:01.869
Nancy Pelosi and Bill Clinton,

00:04:01.869 --> 00:04:04.371
and you know, he had just had a

00:04:04.505 --> 00:04:06.640
fall that week a few days

00:04:06.774 --> 00:04:07.875
earlier.

00:04:07.975 --> 00:04:10.845
Gashed his forehead, had many

00:04:10.978 --> 00:04:11.879
stitches, but he was determined

00:04:11.879 --> 00:04:12.980
to make the event, and he sat

00:04:13.113 --> 00:04:16.383
there in a wheelchair, and

00:04:16.517 --> 00:04:17.084
greeted each and every one of

00:04:17.218 --> 00:04:19.086
us, and spent a few minutes

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:20.754
talking to everyone.

00:04:20.888 --> 00:04:23.290
He just has an amazing stamina

00:04:23.424 --> 00:04:25.159
and love of life.

00:04:25.292 --> 00:04:28.028
He's an incredible force of

00:04:28.162 --> 00:04:28.362
nation.

00:04:28.495 --> 00:04:29.897
&gt;&gt; Yeah, I think that's a really

00:04:29.897 --> 00:04:31.498
good way, he's an incredible

00:04:31.899 --> 00:04:33.968
force of nature, he does it with

00:04:34.101 --> 00:04:36.570
such kindness and compassion.

00:04:36.704 --> 00:04:37.972
It really is remarkable.

00:04:38.105 --> 00:04:39.907
A little bit about his sort of

00:04:39.907 --> 00:04:40.541
family history.

00:04:40.975 --> 00:04:44.044
I understand that pancreatic

00:04:44.178 --> 00:04:46.413
cancer ended up killing many of

00:04:46.547 --> 00:04:48.349
his close relatives, but not Mr.

00:04:48.482 --> 00:04:48.682
Carter.

00:04:48.816 --> 00:04:51.585
How do you think all of this has

00:04:51.919 --> 00:04:52.319
impacted his life, having seen

00:04:52.453 --> 00:04:53.921
others go through cancer and

00:04:53.921 --> 00:04:55.356
dying from it?

00:04:55.489 --> 00:04:57.925
&gt;&gt; Yeah, you know, all of his

00:04:58.058 --> 00:04:59.927
father, Ms. Lilian, his mother,

00:04:59.927 --> 00:05:02.296
all of his siblings, incoming

00:05:02.429 --> 00:05:04.965
Billy Carter, they all died of

00:05:05.099 --> 00:05:05.966
pancreatic cancer.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.269
It was rather unusual, so

00:05:08.402 --> 00:05:09.470
unusual that the national health

00:05:09.603 --> 00:05:10.738
institute made a study of the

00:05:10.871 --> 00:05:12.740
family to figure out what was

00:05:12.873 --> 00:05:13.107
going on.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:18.078
But he escaped this cancer.

00:05:18.212 --> 00:05:19.947
And has led a very vigorous

00:05:19.947 --> 00:05:21.548
life.

00:05:21.949 --> 00:05:22.816
He did come down with melanoma

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:23.951
in 2015.

00:05:24.051 --> 00:05:26.086
Just as I was beginning my

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.188
biography, the outlier, on him.

00:05:28.322 --> 00:05:29.957
And he had this, if you recall,

00:05:29.957 --> 00:05:33.127
he had this amazing press

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.395
conference live at the Carter

00:05:34.528 --> 00:05:38.365
center, where he got up on

00:05:38.499 --> 00:05:42.069
stage, and gave the news very

00:05:42.202 --> 00:05:45.606
calmly, rationally, said that he

00:05:45.973 --> 00:05:46.440
had brain cancer, melanoma that

00:05:46.573 --> 00:05:47.975
had spread from his liver, and

00:05:47.975 --> 00:05:50.311
he probably had just a few weeks

00:05:50.444 --> 00:05:50.644
to live.

00:05:50.778 --> 00:05:53.614
Well, of course we all know he

00:05:53.981 --> 00:05:55.015
then got immune therapy and

00:05:55.149 --> 00:05:58.619
survived and beat the cancer.

00:05:58.752 --> 00:06:02.156
He is a survivor.

00:06:02.289 --> 00:06:02.423
So.

00:06:02.556 --> 00:06:03.991
&gt;&gt; He's a remarkable person.

00:06:04.024 --> 00:06:06.193
Would you agree with a lot of

00:06:06.327 --> 00:06:07.995
the assessment, you know, he's

00:06:08.028 --> 00:06:09.496
still here with us.

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:11.999
He's still living, he has been

00:06:11.999 --> 00:06:12.733
through I don't know how many

00:06:12.866 --> 00:06:14.435
different things that for many

00:06:14.568 --> 00:06:16.003
people has been the end for

00:06:16.003 --> 00:06:18.339
them, but he has survived it.

00:06:18.472 --> 00:06:20.341
75 years of marriage, as you

00:06:20.474 --> 00:06:23.344
mentioned, and that was in 2021,

00:06:23.477 --> 00:06:24.011
did you say?

00:06:24.011 --> 00:06:26.814
&gt;&gt; 2021, right.

00:06:26.947 --> 00:06:28.782
So that was 18 months ago.

00:06:28.916 --> 00:06:30.217
&gt;&gt; And we're looking at

00:06:30.351 --> 00:06:32.019
pictures, I think, of his

00:06:32.019 --> 00:06:32.720
family, which is quite large,

00:06:32.853 --> 00:06:34.221
and they're all laughing, and

00:06:34.355 --> 00:06:35.122
they're all sharing time

00:06:35.255 --> 00:06:35.489
together.

00:06:35.622 --> 00:06:39.159
But I do want to ask you

00:06:39.293 --> 00:06:40.427
about -- a little bit about him

00:06:40.561 --> 00:06:42.496
and post presidency, most people

00:06:42.629 --> 00:06:45.299
when they think of Jimmy Carter,

00:06:45.432 --> 00:06:46.433
he was a one-term president,

00:06:46.567 --> 00:06:49.436
which in the political world is

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:50.971
not necessarily the most

00:06:51.105 --> 00:06:52.039
successful presidency, but in

00:06:52.039 --> 00:06:56.143
the life after wards.

00:06:56.276 --> 00:06:57.511
He's done remarkable things that

00:06:57.644 --> 00:06:59.113
have impacted people's lives.

00:06:59.246 --> 00:07:03.450
Can you talk a little bit about

00:07:03.584 --> 00:07:04.051
that.

00:07:04.051 --> 00:07:06.286
&gt;&gt; I argue in my biography, his

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:07.354
presidency, his four years was

00:07:07.488 --> 00:07:10.057
quite successful.

00:07:10.057 --> 00:07:10.457
He accomplished quite a bit.

00:07:10.591 --> 00:07:14.061
But I also wrote that he sort of

00:07:14.061 --> 00:07:15.129
tongue and cheek was the only

00:07:15.262 --> 00:07:16.263
president who used the white

00:07:16.397 --> 00:07:18.732
house as a stepping-stone to

00:07:18.866 --> 00:07:20.434
greater things.

00:07:20.567 --> 00:07:22.669
And it's true, you know, he had

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:26.140
a remarkable ex-presidency.

00:07:26.273 --> 00:07:28.375
Just a continuation of his

00:07:28.509 --> 00:07:31.145
presidency in many ways, doing

00:07:31.278 --> 00:07:32.613
good works, so, you know, he

00:07:32.746 --> 00:07:34.148
often joked that at the Carter

00:07:34.281 --> 00:07:36.683
center that he wanted to live

00:07:36.817 --> 00:07:41.588
longer than the last Guinea

00:07:41.722 --> 00:07:43.724
worm, and the Carter center has

00:07:44.091 --> 00:07:46.427
spent decades now, wiping occupy

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:48.829
millions of cases of Guinea worm

00:07:48.962 --> 00:07:50.097
disease, a terrible affliction,

00:07:50.097 --> 00:07:52.132
and they're now, I think, in

00:07:52.266 --> 00:07:56.103
2022, we're only 13 cases in

00:07:56.103 --> 00:07:57.438
human beings of Guinea worm

00:07:57.571 --> 00:08:00.107
disease so he's almost made it.

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:01.608
&gt;&gt; Thank you so much for sharing

00:08:01.742 --> 00:08:02.643
your insights.

00:08:02.776 --> 00:08:05.412
You're the author of "The

00:08:05.546 --> 00:08:08.916
outlier, the unfinished

